{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04S9", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-2-category-fibred-sets}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d38b9963a459b96239864a51ea675c904a745b7e20eedecf35513be44ec6c55e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus categories fibred in setoids are exactly the categories fibred\nin groupoids which are equivalent to categories fibred in sets.\nMoreover, an equivalence of categories fibred in sets is an isomorphism\nby Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f02901b7d52e997cff4a78fad1fab24de4b0598b1f0fd9f1fd9732338882e244", "unit_id": "tag:04S9:prose-0004"}
